//
// One row group (handoff LAYOUT.md §"Content — row groups"): an optional
// uppercase caption, a rounded `subtle` body holding the rows, and an
// optional footnote below it.
//
// The rows arrive through a SLOT rather than as props, because a group's rows
// are heterogeneous (toggle / value / select / chevron) and a slot body is
// lexically the CALLER's — that is what lets a section write
// `Toggle { checked: $state.tgWifi }` inside a row and still get the DSL's
// automatic two-way binding, which only fires on a `$state` ref at the widget
// itself.
//
// Caption type is `xs` (11px) where the handoff says 10.5px: the baked type
// ramp has no step below 11 (recorded non-parity, TASK-0308).
//
// NO `.overflow(hidden)` on the body, even though the handoff clips its rows
// to the group's radius: a hidden-overflow container passes its own CLIPPED
// constraints down (engine.rs), and with no explicit height that resolved to
// zero — the boot showed three group captions and no rows at all. The corners
// therefore do not clip the first and last row.

Component SetGroup {
    props: {
        label: Str,
        note: Str,
    }
    slot rows
    Stack {
        if $props.label != "" {
            Text($props.label).textSize(xs).fontWeight(semibold).fg(onGlassMuted)
        } else {
            Stack { }
        }
        Stack {
            Slot rows
        }
        .gap(0)
        .rounded(xl)
        .material(subtle)
        if $props.note != "" {
            Text($props.note).textSize(xs).leading(normal).fg(onGlassMuted)
        } else {
            Stack { }
        }
    }
    .gap(2)
}
